#
#  Vtable for RRFS v1 (FV3-LAM) CONUS 3 km GRIB2 output, as the NAM replacement
#  boundary/initial-condition source for the DrJack WRF chain (RRFS_MIGRATION.md).
#
#  Feed ungrib BOTH files for each valid time (link them together as GRIBFILE.*):
#    rrfs.tCCz.prslev.3km.fFFF.conus.grib2  -> isobaric TT/UU/VV/RH/HGT (45 levels)
#    rrfs.tCCz.2dfld.3km.fFFF.conus.grib2   -> everything on level types 1/101/103/106
#
#  Differences from Vtable.NAM:
#    * Soil: RRFS writes RUC-LSM soil at 9 single depths (0,1,4,10,30,60,100,160,300 cm),
#      GRIB2 level 106 with top == bottom, exactly like RAP/HRRR -> the Vtable.raphrrr
#      soil block (GRIB1 level type 111, single depth) replaces NAM's 4 layer pairs
#      (type 112). real.exe interpolates these onto Noah's 4 layers.
#    * Sea-level pressure: RRFS has MSLET only (0/3/192). Same code Vtable.NAM uses.
#  Everything else is byte-identical NCEP GRIB2 coding, so no other changes.
#
#  Not extracted on purpose: p-level hydrometeors (CLMR 0/1/22, ICMR 0/1/23 - NOT CICE,
#  RWMR 0/1/24, SNMR 0/1/25, GRLE 0/1/32). The NAM chain never used them; add a QC/QI/...
#  block modelled on Vtable.HRRR.full (with ICMR = 0/1/23) to experiment with cloud init.
#
